Here we go again... I've been doing a bit of work on the design of an OOP
nethack, and there's one thing I just can decide: How do you model item /
item interactions? For example, dipping a unicorn horn in a potion. If it's
healing, nothing happens. If it's hallucination, the potion turns to water.
Which object should contain this knowledge? This gets even more difficult
if you're not sure what all the objects in the game are, as we were
discussing previously.

A visitor-pattern style double-dispatch seems too restrictive to me. Perhaps
a registry of interactions, storing the first item, the action, the second
item, and a function to call when that happens... Would be tedious, though.


